  "createdAt": "2026-10-07T15:07:58.503Z",
  "controllerObservations": [
    "Lila v1 direction insufficiently sideward; v2 is a targeted head/chest-direction edit, not an approved replacement.",
    "AI atlas has nonuniform foot placement and subtle head/body/garment drift. Explicit per-position anchors only address frame origin, not internal anatomy or scale drift.",
    "Gemini static advice found peak-extension stroke thinning, garment contour variation, foot spacing/ground and shoulder-anchor drift in Lila v2/Karo v1.",
    "Latest v3/v2 use a targeted master-body consistency edit; neither guarantees exact copied identity or limb length.",
    "Manual corrected alpha-128 selections have no occupied pixels at their frame edges. Lila occupancy height 305-306px; Karo 255-258px. These are pixel observations, not anatomical contact, native timing or approval.",
    "Initial Karo row boundary crossed occupied pixels; corrected selection uses transparent bands. Worksheet v1 also let adjacent PNG rows spill visually; v2 uses explicit native clips. Historical artifacts remain superseded evidence.",
    "Gemini advice v2 still reports limb/cloth/rest drift. Its crisp angular elbow suggestion is rejected because the user requires soft drawn contours; limb length and natural bend constraints remain applicable.",
    "User reports no local image-to-video API. Production motion must be authored through the available code/art workflow; this is not a reason to replace actors with a slideshow."
  ],
  "updatedAt": "2026-10-07T16:14:04.854Z"
